          "distinct": true,
          "id": "4d1caf2504747dc7b183b30c6f2f74ec3a3dd105",
          "message": "fix(#706): return live module globals dict from globals() (#810)\n\n`globals()` was returning a fresh snapshot dict on every call. This meant\nmutations to the returned dict were not visible as module globals, and\n`g is globals()` returned False.\n\n**interpreter.rs**: Added a `module_globals_dict: Value` field — a single\npersistent `Value::dict(...)` that `globals()` returns on every call. All\nmodule-level assignments write into this dict via `assign_name` so it stays\nlive.\n\n**program.rs**: Switched module execution to all-env mode (empty `local_index`).\nWith an empty local_index the compiler emits `StoreGlobal` for every module-level\nassignment instead of writing to a fastlocal register. `StoreGlobal` calls\n`assign_name` which writes to both `env.values` AND `module_globals_dict`, keeping\nthe dict live. Also mirrors the standard module dunders into `module_globals_dict`\nduring `seed_module_dunders`.\n\n**env.rs**: `assign_name` now also writes to `module_globals_dict` at module scope\n(both the `is_global` function-level path and the fall-through module-scope path).\n\n**vm.rs**: `LoadGlobal` now checks the env chain (`lookup_name`) FIRST, then falls\nback to `module_globals_dict`. This is the correct order: function-level cell vars\nand nonlocal bindings live in the env chain and must not be shadowed by a same-named\nmodule global in the dict. `module_globals_dict` is only needed as a fallback for\nnames inserted via `globals()[\"x\"] = val` that bypass `assign_name`. `DeleteName`\nalso removes from `module_globals_dict` so deleted names are not resurrected.\n\n**builtins.rs**: `globals()` returns `module_globals_dict.clone()` (same Rc, so\nidentity is preserved). `locals()` at module scope likewise returns\n`module_globals_dict.clone()` since at module scope locals == globals.\n\n**optimizer.rs**: Fixed `pass_binopinplace_downgrade` not to downgrade\n`BinOpInPlace` when `num_locals == 0` (all-env module scope). In all-env mode\nevery register is a \"temp\" (>= num_locals=0), so the existing guard\n`lhs >= num_locals` always fired — including for user-defined objects with\n`__imatmul__` etc., causing `x @= y` to call `__matmul__` instead.\n\n**Self-review caught:**\n\n1. Initial `LoadGlobal` rewrite checked `module_globals_dict` BEFORE `lookup_name`,\n   which caused a nonlocal variable `g` (in `inc` with `nonlocal g`) to incorrectly\n   read from module-level `g` instead of the enclosing function's env. Fixed by\n   restoring the correct priority: env chain first, dict second.\n\n2. The `BinOpInPlace` downgrade in the optimizer fired unconditionally in all-env\n   mode because `num_locals == 0` makes every register look like a temp. Added\n   `num_locals > 0` guard to the downgrade condition.\n\n- New parity fixture: `crates/pyrust/tests/cases/runtime/test_globals_live.py`\n  (identity, live-view, dict-write, locals-is-globals, imatmul, del, nonlocal-shadow)\n- `cargo test --release --bin pyrust` → 319 passed\n- `cargo test --release --test parity_compare` → 1 passed (all cases green)",
