          "message": "perf(#810): lazy module_globals_dict sync; StrKey in LoadGlobal fallback (#814)\n\nPR #810 added an eager mirror write to module_globals_dict inside\nassign_name for every module-scope StoreGlobal, and searched the dict\non every LoadGlobal miss with PyKey::Str(name.to_string()) — allocating\na heap String on each probe.  Together these caused a ~15x regression on\ntight loops that do not use globals() (test_while_cmp went from 3.7x\nfaster than CPython to 3.4x slower).\n\nFix:\n\n* Add `globals_accessed: bool` to `Interpreter` (default false).\n* `assign_name` now skips the module_globals_dict write until\n  `globals_accessed` is set — eliminating the extra IndexMap write on\n  every assignment for scripts that never call globals().\n* `globals()` and `locals()` (module scope) call\n  `sync_module_env_to_globals_dict`: sets the flag and does a one-time\n  bulk copy of env.values → dict, after which assign_name resumes\n  mirroring so the live-view semantics (issue #706) are preserved.\n* `LoadGlobal` dict fallback now uses `StrKey(name)` instead of\n  `PyKey::Str(name.to_string())`, eliminating a heap allocation on\n  every lookup that misses the env chain.\n\nAll existing parity tests pass, including test_globals_live.py which\ncovers the identity, live-view, dict-write-as-global, and\nlocals-is-globals invariants.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-20T10:44:43+09:00",
          "tree_id": "f44730f3eb983c5871e131160ee92b7587fd2b8f",
          "url": "https://github.com/ChanyaVRC/pyrust/commit/45b2abc6147d2c0c0cce9fb1120487958991c460"
