          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e4cba678b4acf4d8258a4c0146fd082821b707e9",
          "message": "fix(#947 review): add copy.error backward-compat alias (#950)\n\nCPython's copy.py has `error = Error` for backward compatibility;\n`copy.error is copy.Error` is True in CPython 3.12.  The initial\nimplementation only exported `copy.Error`, causing `copy.error` to\nraise AttributeError.\n\nAdd \"error\" => copy_error_class_value() to the constants block so\nboth names resolve to the same thread-local Rc, making identity\nchecks pass.  Extend the parity fixture to cover both names.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-21T19:02:17+09:00",
          "tree_id": "ca3ec44c4a64610e98e824b91286b580a5fac6a9",
