          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e51f22a19055acfdfb1258aaa4445cf4dbf2997b",
          "message": "fix(#959): sys.version_info.__qualname__ should be 'version_info' not 'sys.version_info' (#960)\n\n* fix(#957): append '(unknown location)' to from-import AttributeError messages\n\nCPython 3.12 appends '(unknown location)' to ImportError messages from\n'from mod import name' when the module has no __file__ (C extensions,\nbuilt-in modules). pyrust has no physical paths for any module, so the\nsuffix was always omitted. Appended unconditionally to the ImportFromAttr\nerror message, matching CPython's fallback for path-less modules.\n\n* fix(#957): remove math from parity fixture (has .so path on Linux CI)\n\n* fix(#959): sys.version_info.__qualname__ should be 'version_info' not 'sys.version_info'\n\nSame module-qualification bug as #955 (copy.Error.__qualname__). The\nVERSION_INFO_CLASS thread-local had qualname set to 'sys.version_info'\ninstead of 'version_info'. Added assertion to the existing parity fixture.",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-21T19:46:31+09:00",
