          "distinct": true,
          "id": "a53f3c5e41b7d8f0fbbfa16f761319ef2e07762d",
          "message": "fix(#965): float modulo sign for zero results with negative divisor (#967)\n\n## Summary\n\n`0.0 % -3.0` returned `0.0` in pyrust but CPython 3.12 gives `-0.0`.\nThe bug existed in both the slow path (`expr.rs::modulo`) and the fast\npath (`vm.rs::float_float_fast`).\n\n## What Changed\n\nCPython's `float_rem` uses `fmod()` then applies `copysign(0.0, wx)` to\na zero result, and `+= wx` when the result sign disagrees with the\ndivisor sign.\n\n- `expr.rs::modulo` float path: replaced the `a - b * (a / b).floor()`\n  formula with `a % b` (Rust's fmod) followed by the same two-step\n  sign correction.\n- `vm.rs::float_float_fast` `BinOp::Mod` arm: the non-zero sign\n  adjustment was already present but the zero case (copysign) was\n  missing; added the missing branch.\n\n## Self-review caught\n\nThe fast path in vm.rs had the non-zero sign adjustment written as an\nexplicit `(r > 0.0 && b < 0.0) || (r < 0.0 && b > 0.0)` condition.\nThe zero case was absent, causing the bug. The fix adds a unified\n`if r == 0.0 { copysign } else if signum mismatch { += b }` form\nconsistent with the slow path.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `0.0 % -3.0` → `-0.0` (the reported bug)\n- `0.0 % 3.0` → `0.0` (regression guard)\n- `7.0 % -3.0` → `-2.0`, `-7.0 % 3.0` → `2.0` (non-zero cases)\n- `6.0 % -3.0` → `-0.0` (exact multiple with negative divisor)\n- ZeroDivisionError still raised for `1.0 % 0.0`\n- Parity fixture verified byte-identical under python3.12\n- `cargo test --release --workspace` and `cargo test --release --test parity_compare` both green",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-25T18:34:23+09:00",
          "tree_id": "4dc24795ce0e197dc9a3153144a5341e12ba2027",
