          "distinct": true,
          "id": "e70af1d13e0a7af2000e73f852256661111d298d",
          "message": "fix(#966): ForCountConstInline back-edge offset for nested loops (#968)\n\n* fix(#966): ForCountConstInline back-edge offset for nested loops\n\n## Summary\n\n`pass_thread_jumps` was following backward `Jump` instructions (loop\nback-edges) when threading the exit offset of `ForCount*` instructions.\nFor nested `for i in range(N): for j in range(M):` loops, the inner\nloop's exit was threaded through the outer loop's backward back-edge\n`Jump`, landing at the outer loop header — a lower address than the\ninner loop header itself.  This produced a negative `off` in the inner\n`ForCountConst` / `ForCountConstInline`, violating the invariant that\nthe exit offset is always positive (pointing past the loop body).\n\n## What Changed\n\n`pass_thread_jumps` — the `follow` helper — now stops at any `Jump`\nwith a negative offset (backward jump / loop back-edge).  Only forward\n`Jump` chains (offset ≥ 0) are followed.  This preserves all existing\nforward-chain threading while preventing the backward-threading that\ncorrupted nested-loop exit offsets.\n\nThe guard comment in `pass_forcount_unroll` (the `off_i32 < 2`\nearly-continue) is updated to reflect that negative offsets should no\nlonger occur; the guard now reads as a structural sanity check for the\nempty-body (`off == 1`) case rather than a workaround for corrupted\nbytecode.\n\n## Self-review caught\n\nConfirmed via debug-instrumented build that the negative `off` appeared\nimmediately after `pass_thread_jumps` in the pipeline, before any other\npass touched the instruction.  The root cause was unambiguously in the\n`follow` helper, not in LICM, dead-code elimination, or any later pass.\n\nVerified 2-level and 3-level nested loops, empty inner body, and\nnon-trivial inner body all produce correct output matching CPython 3.12.\n\n## Test plan\n\n- New parity fixture `test_nested_for_range.py` covers 2-level with\n  body, 2-level print, 3-level, and empty inner body.\n- `cargo test --release --workspace` — 385 + parity tests, all green.\n- `cargo test --release --test parity_compare` — green.\n\n* fix(#968 review): add unit test for backward-jump stop in pass_thread_jumps\n\nThe existing thread_jumps tests covered chain collapsing, self-loop\ncycle prevention, and the no-op case, but none verified the new guard\nthat stops follow() at backward jumps (the root fix for issue #966).\n\nAdd thread_jumps_stops_at_backward_jump: constructs a minimal nested-\nloop bytecode layout (ForCountConstInline + inner back-edge + outer\nback-edge) and asserts that the ForCountConstInline exit offset remains\nnon-negative after threading. Before the fix, follow() would have\nthreaded through the outer Jump(-4) back-edge and produced off = -1.",
