          "distinct": true,
          "id": "1cfb208cbb20dcf103805d1339bfb86203c1a543",
          "message": "fix(#648): document active-script-frame noalias fix; add locals/globals parity fixture (#969)\n\n## Summary\n\nIssue #648 identified that `run_bytecode_inner_impl`'s former `regs: &mut [Value]`\nparameter asserted LLVM noalias on the script-frame register buffer while\n`VmFrameView::regs_ptr` still pointed into the same allocation. The fix\n(replacing `&mut [Value]` with `RegSlice` in every dispatch-loop signature)\nwas already applied as part of PR #646 / issue #547; this commit completes\nthe issue by:\n\n## What Changed\n\n- Updated SAFETY comment in `program.rs` (the active-script-frame push site)\n  to explicitly call out issue #648 alongside #547, and explain that both the\n  VmFrameView push and the RegSlice construction share the same raw pointer with\n  no `&mut [Value]` in scope, covering the `locals()`/`globals()` read path.\n\n- Updated `RegSlice` doc comment in `interpreter.rs` to reference issue #648\n  in addition to #547.\n\n- Added parity fixture `test_locals_script_scope.py` (required by the issue's\n  acceptance criteria) covering:\n  - `locals()` at module/script scope returning in-flight fastlocal registers\n  - `globals()` from inside a nested function seeing the module namespace\n  - `locals()` inside a module-level generator\n\n## Test plan\n\n- `cargo test --release --workspace` — all 385+ tests pass\n- `cargo test --release --test parity_compare` — parity fixture matches CPython 3.12\n- Manual check: `x = 1; assert locals()['x'] == 1` passes under both runtimes",
          "timestamp": "2026-05-25T19:10:23+09:00",
          "tree_id": "d3659cd80181d355068c0d3871e0c29babdf7f06",
